{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+ & Gram-", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "Unknown", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals this sequence is most similar (93.1%) to frog Palustrin-2GN3 A single residue variant. L=21%, K=17%. GRAVY: 0.417; M Wt: 2943.59; Mol formula: C129H232N36O37S2; Mol ex coeff: 125. Activity: active against E. coli ATCC 25922 (MIC 2-4 ug/ml), S. enteritidis (MIC 16-32 ug/ml), and S. aureus ATCC 29213 (MIC 4-8 ug/ml). In vitro Toxicity: porcine RBC HC50 64-128 ug/ml.", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "35884206", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Antibiotics (Basel). 2022 Jul 15;11(7):952. doi: 10.3390/antibiotics11070952. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP03514", "source_id": "AP03514", "source_numeric_id": "03514", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP03514", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "Mining Amphibian and Insect Transcriptomes for Antimicrobial Peptide Sequences with rAMPage", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
